      "exact_frozen_census_obligation": "W03 records the project chronology as a succession of Euclidean-twistor, right-handed-spacetime, and July-2026 Wick-rotation/chiral-field stages; these are revision relations, not one timeless formulation. The dated October 20, 2022 W03 proposal explicitly claims Euclidean twistor geometry can host Standard Model and chiral-gravity degrees of freedom without newly exotic fields, with one chiral SU(2) internal and an imaginary-time choice associated with electroweak breaking. Its eight listed attractive aspects source-assert tautological Weyl spinors as spacetime points, shared Minkowski/Euclidean twistor complexification for analytic continuation, EXACTLY Standard Model internal symmetries, a broken-Euclidean-SO(4) source of EWSB, simple one-generation fermion transformation construction, new chiral gravity in a Standard Model unification proposal, fundamental conformal symmetry, and the p=infinity Fargues-Fontaine arithmetic analogy. These are author-claimed merits of the unfinished proposal, not verified theorems, equivalences or a completed unification. The page also gives an 1988 embryonic antecedent, April/October 2021 paper revision sequence, dated talks and a W05 P1-related citation without importing their semantics. On October 30, 2023 it explicitly narrows to right-handed spinor geometry as sufficient for spacetime degrees of freedom in a short new paper with Euclidean/Minkowski signature contrast; this later update is not the timeless identity of the 2022 formulation.",
